<%#
  THE section header: the one Ticketing settings draws (Tim, 2026-10-12 —
  "the best one"). A white strip at the top of a white card: the title in
  bold, an optional gray line under it, anything for the right side
  (buttons, a Pro pill) in the block, and a hairline between it and the
  card's body. It replaced the old gray-bar card_header (deleted) and
  shared/section_header's look everywhere. A card that has no background
  of its own gets bg-white, so the strip and the body read as one.

    render "shared/section_heading", title: "Production details"
    render "shared/section_heading", title: "Documents", intro: "Shared with your cast." do
      ...buttons...
    end

  Locals: title, intro (optional), padding (optional, default "px-6 py-4";
  pass e.g. "px-4 py-3" to line up with a card body's p-4), icon (optional
  SVG markup shown before the title, e.g. a location pin).
%>
<% right = block_given? ? capture { yield } : nil %>
<div class="<%= local_assigns[:padding] || 'px-6 py-4' %> border-b border-gray-200 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3">
  <div class="min-w-0">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900<%= ' flex items-center gap-2' if local_assigns[:icon] %>"><%= local_assigns[:icon]&.html_safe %><%= title %></h2>
    <% if local_assigns[:intro].present? %><p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1"><%= intro %></p><% end %>
  </div>
  <% if right.present? && right.strip.present? %>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2"><%= right %></div>
  <% end %>
</div>
